{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"title":"Sending batches"},{"anchor":"Encoding-a-batch","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch"],"title":"Encoding a batch"},{"anchor":"Reading-a-2xx-answer","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportResponse"],"title":"Reading a 2xx answer"},{"anchor":"Splitting-a-batch-into-requests","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchRequests","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/SkippedRecord"],"title":"Splitting a batch into requests"},{"anchor":"Retrying-a-vendors-own-statuses","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/TransientStatus","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidTransientStatus"],"title":"Retrying a vendor’s own statuses"},{"anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry"],"title":"Waiting between attempts"},{"anchor":"Sending-requests","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError"],"title":"Sending requests"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as the requests its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" splits it into: one request for an endpoint without limits. Each body is whatever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the encoder writes for its records, so events need no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance and the wire format is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yours. It sends with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" by default, or through any "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" you pass."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": nominally 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is one answered with a status the encoder lists in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder declares: empty for most servers, or each other failure its vendor answers to a request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"worth sending again, such as Aptabase’s 418 for a slow upload."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A 2xx counts as delivered unless the encoder’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" reads its body and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"says otherwise. Some vendors answer 200 to a request they didn’t store, and say so only in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"body: Mixpanel’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"status\": 0}"},{"type":"text","text":", or Aptabase’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"error\": ...}"},{"type":"text","text":" for an unknown key. A 2xx the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder reads as "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/rejected(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is dropped and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport\/rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":". One it reads as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/transient(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent again under the same backoff and deadline as a 5xx."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"An encoder should count an empty body, or one it can’t read, as delivered, so an answer it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t recognize never sends a request again and again; the DestinationTesting conformance kit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checks that it does. A transient answer is retried until the request’s deadline, so an encoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose requests have none should return rejected instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each wait has full jitter by default: a random wait shorter than the nominal one, so apps refused"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at the same moment retry at different moments. Pass "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum\/none","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nominal waits. In tests, pass a seeded generator as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"randomNumberGenerator:"},{"type":"text","text":" for jittered waits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that repeat from one run to the next, as long as one request retries at a time: copies of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination retrying at once share the generator’s draws in the order they ask for them. Never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"seed it in production, where every device would then wait the same, which defeats the jitter. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", as is each record the encoder leaves out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its requests. So is a request still undelivered at its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder sets for a vendor that misdates or ignores old events: the destination checks it on its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"now:"},{"type":"text","text":" clock before every attempt and sends nothing more once it has passed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of each request’s first record into its header"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, give the destination a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"text":"); for PostHog,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"make it with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken:host:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Amplitude, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Mixpanel, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelEncoding"},{"text":");","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.segment(writeKey:region:plan:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:)"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},{"text":"); for Google Analytics 4, from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"server, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"},{"text":"); for Snowplow, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SnowplowEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryDeck, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:)"},{"text":" (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"},{"text":"); for Matomo, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MatomoEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Heap, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.heap(appID:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeapEncoding"},{"text":"); for Aptabase, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AptabaseEncoding"},{"text":"). To read events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inside the app or in a test, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destinations"},{"text":") instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","","struct PlansEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    static let transientStatuses: Set<TransientStatus> = []","","    static func outcome(of response: HTTPTransportResponse, for request: EncodedRequest) -> ResponseOutcome {","        .delivered","    }","","    func requests(for batch: [EventRecord]) -> BatchRequests<Never> {","        let plans = batch.compactMap { ($0.event as? SignedUp)?.plan }","        let body = EncodedBatch(body: Data(plans.joined(separator: \"\\n\").utf8), contentType: \"text\/plain\")","        return BatchRequests(requests: [EncodedRequest(body: body, recordIDs: batch.map(\\.id))], skippedRecords: [])","    }","}","","let server = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: endpointURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder(),","    backoff: try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(2), maximumDelay: .seconds(120)))","let drops = server.dropReports","let watching = Task {","    for await drop in drops {","        print(\"Dropped a batch: \\(drop)\")","    }","}","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: server)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers this destination beside the others, and what a delivery does while a batch is retried.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"HTTPDestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations","role":"collection"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations"]}],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPTransportResponse":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPTransportResponse"}],"role":"symbol","title":"HTTPTransportResponse","abstract":[{"text":"What an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","type":"reference"},{"text":" received for a request: the response’s status and header fields, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its body.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPTransportResponse"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportResponse","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httptransportresponse"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/EncodedRequest/deadline":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deadline","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","text":"Date","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/encodedrequest\/deadline","kind":"symbol","title":"deadline","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The latest wall-clock time at which the request may be sent, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when it may be sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at any time."}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ResponseOutcome":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResponseOutcome"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResponseOutcome"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/responseoutcome","role":"symbol","title":"ResponseOutcome","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a successful (2xx) answer to a request means, as its "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" reads the answer’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"body ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/TransientStatus":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TransientStatus"}],"role":"symbol","title":"TransientStatus","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A failure status that "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" retries, beside 408 Request Timeout, 429 Too Many"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Requests and every 5xx, for an encoder that lists it in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TransientStatus"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/TransientStatus","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/transientstatus","type":"topic"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPTransport":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httptransport","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPTransport"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPTransport"}],"title":"HTTPTransport","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"What sends an HTTP request and returns the server’s response: the seam between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and the network.","type":"text"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchRequests":{"kind":"symbol","title":"BatchRequests","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchRequests","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchRequests"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchRequests"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A batch as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" encodes it: the requests that carry its records, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the records it left out."}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchrequests"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","title":"Choosing Destinations","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Choosing Destinations","type":"text"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDropReport/rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport\/rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rejectedInBody","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"status","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPResponse","preciseIdentifier":"s:9HTTPTypes12HTTPResponseV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Status","preciseIdentifier":"s:9HTTPTypes12HTTPResponseV6StatusV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reason","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"recordIDs","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"UUID","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4UUIDV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdropreport\/rejectedinbody(status:reason:recordids:)","role":"symbol","title":"HTTPDropReport.rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The endpoint answered with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"status"},{"type":"text","text":", a 2xx, but the answer’s body says the vendor stored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none of the records and won’t if they are sent again ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/rejected(reason:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reason"},{"type":"text","text":", so the batch of the records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identified by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recordIDs"},{"type":"text","text":", oldest first, was dropped. Mixpanel’s track API, answering 200"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"status\": 0, \"error\": ...}"},{"type":"text","text":", is one such vendor."}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/NonPositiveRetry":{"abstract":[{"text":"The error ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/delay(beforeRetry:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" throws for a retry numbered below 1.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry","title":"NonPositiveRetry","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NonPositiveRetry","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/nonpositiveretry","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NonPositiveRetry","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/EncodedBatch":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EncodedBatch","kin